# rlroz.msg - Roz Mercer, madam of the Silver Garter (New Reno)
# Plain ASCII only: the English Fallout 2 fonts have no umlauts or typographic quotes.

# Report and payout
{100}{}{The cards don't lie. Only the people holding them do. Here's the week.}
{121}{}{. Count it. Everybody in this town counts twice.}
{122}{}{Nothing. The families ate first. They always eat first.}

# Prices and share
{130}{}{New Reno pays for what it can brag about. Cheap gets you drunks who don't pay. Dear gets you men who think they bought the room.}
{140}{}{Our people keep }
{141}{}{ percent of what they bring in. Every house on Virgin Street takes more, and every house on Virgin Street has girls who steal.}
{145}{}{A quarter. (She shrugs.) Then they'll steal the rest. I'll just have to count faster.}
{146}{}{A third. That's the Virgin Street price. Nobody's happy, nobody runs.}
{147}{}{Almost half? (She raises an eyebrow.) Kitty will hate you. The girls will love you. Both of those are useful.}

# Morale
{150}{}{They're sharp. They laugh at the right jokes and remember the wrong ones. That's a good house.}
{151}{}{They work. They drink after. It's New Reno.}
{152}{}{They're quiet. In this town, quiet means somebody is counting how much it costs to leave.}
{153}{}{Two of them keep looking at the door. One has a bag packed under her bed. I can see it from here.}

# Crisis: the drug
{160}{}{One of ours is chasing Jet. In New Reno that's like saying one of ours is breathing. But she's stealing from the till to do it.}
{165}{}{(Roz watches you work.) I've seen doctors in this town. None of them did that for free.}
{166}{}{I'll take her to somebody who doesn't sell the stuff on the side. If there's anybody like that left.}
{167}{}{(Roz shrugs.) Half the houses on Virgin Street pay in Jet. The girls stay. They stop being people, but they stay.}
{168}{}{Out she goes. One of Big Jesus' boys will have her selling on a corner by morning.}

# Look
{200}{}{A woman in her forties with dealer's hands and eyes that count everything in the room.}
{201}{}{Roz Mercer. Ten years dealing cards at the Shark Club. Now she deals the Silver Garter.}

# Construction and staff (her voice)
{460}{}{What do we build? In New Reno, people pay to be seen. So we build something worth being seen in.}
{463}{}{Something you only get in New Reno.}
{483}{}{Nobody's out looking for new faces.}
{484}{}{Our recruiter works the casinos. The ones who lost everything at the tables come to us. At least here they get paid for losing.}
{485}{}{Our recruiter works at Big Jesus' prices. Debts, Jet, a brother who owes the wrong family. They don't come because they want to.}
{490}{}{I know a croupier at the Desperado who hears every sad story in town. She'll send us the ones who want out of their debts.}
{491}{}{(Roz looks at you for a long moment.) Debt collectors. Fine. It's New Reno. Just don't tell me their names.}

# First meeting
{800}{}{(A woman is shuffling a deck at the bar, fast, without looking at it.) Roz Mercer. Two Chairs said you'd need somebody who can smell a cheat. Ten years at the Shark Club. I've seen every trick, and I've done most of them. The house has rules now: nobody touches the girls without paying, nobody pays in Jet, and nobody cheats at my tables. Except me.}
{801}{}{Show me how the house is doing.}

# The headquarters' treasury, when Asch is dead
{810}{}{Asch's safe. Somebody has to open it now.}
{811}{}{The runners brought $}
{812}{}{. Asch kept it in the safe. The combination was written inside his hat.}

# Blood on Virgin Street, act 3: Jet in the blood
{819}{}{About the Jet in the house.}
{820}{}{Somebody is selling Jet to our people. Two of them already. It's not the girls buying on the street. It's somebody in here.}
{821}{}{It's a new barback. He came recommended from the Desperado. He sells in the storeroom between shifts. What do we do with him?}
{822}{}{(He goes through the front door without touching the steps.) He won't come back. The Desperado will send someone else. They always do.}
{823}{}{(He talks for an hour: who supplies him, who gives the orders, what Venuti wants. He'll keep selling, and he'll tell us everything. It's proof, if we ever need it.)}
{824}{}{(The barback leaves with two men you don't know. Nobody asks. Golgotha doesn't ask either.)}
{825}{}{(Two days of sweat and screaming in the back rooms. The two of them are clean now. For how long, nobody knows.)}
{826}{}{The dealer's gone. The girls he got hooked are still sick.}
{830}{}{[Perception] I'll watch the storeroom.}
{831}{}{[Sneak] I'll follow the new faces after their shift.}
{832}{}{(The girls tell you themselves who it is. People talk when they're treated fairly.)}
{833}{}{[Doctor] Get the girls clean.}
{834}{}{[Unarmed] Throw him out.}
{835}{}{[Speech] Turn him. He works for us now.}
{836}{}{Make him disappear.}

